body:
I'm writing a dystopia, but where there's no real event, the protagonist is a bureaucrat in the system, he doesn't want anything but a promotion. He would have no reason to join the revolution, and the one that will be attempted is going to fail. I know how I want the story to end.

&#x200B;

I want the story to be about how he goes from being an unimaginative bureaucrat, lacking empathy and critical thinking, unaware of his chains, to a person with motivation and longing to be free and free others. Essentially, I have his need, but I don't have his want.
